# Rows of parsed data are laid into objects of a class. The class has the names of the interface, and it is the only layout of the program that has them, so the written type `Row` reaches the engine as
# `Member`: the constructor expected to be handed an object of its own class, a test that failed at every row, with every read by name and all that reckons with them behind a rare edge. Every caller of the
# constructor is known and no Member was seen to arrive: nothing is expected of the parameter.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES: entries-of-bun
# CHECK-NOT: ShapeTest
# CHECK: PropGet {{*}} key="id"
